# Settings for smartclock-web.  See `smartclock-web --help`.
#
# Every line below is commented out and shows the built-in default.
# Uncomment one only to change it.

#SMARTCLOCK_WEB_LISTEN=127.0.0.1:9980

# The daemons' sockets, one instance per subdirectory; the live strip
# follows the selected receiver to its daemon.  Set
# SMARTCLOCK_WEB_DAEMON to list the daemons instead, comma-separated,
# each [NAME=]ENDPOINT: a socket or tcp://HOST:PORT.
#SMARTCLOCK_WEB_RUN_DIR=/run/smartclockd

# The daemons' logs, one per receiver.  Set SMARTCLOCK_WEB_DATABASE to
# a file instead to read one log.
#SMARTCLOCK_WEB_LOG_DIR=/var/lib/smartclockd

# The sensor service's log, and the service itself.
#SMARTCLOCK_WEB_SENSOR_LOG=/var/lib/smartclock-sensord/sensors.sqlite
#SMARTCLOCK_WEB_SENSORD=/run/smartclock-sensord/socket
